    "sampleResponse": "(a) $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac13\\cdot\\frac32\\left(x^2+2\\right)^{1/2}\\cdot2x=x\\sqrt{x^2+2}$. Then $1+\\left(\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right)^2=1+x^2\\left(x^2+2\\right)=x^4+2x^2+1=\\left(x^2+1\\right)^2$.\n(b) Length $=\\int_0^3\\sqrt{\\left(x^2+1\\right)^2}\\,dx=\\int_0^3\\left(x^2+1\\right)dx=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}+x\\right]_0^3=9+3=12$.\n(c) Average value $=\\frac13\\int_0^3\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,dx=\\frac13\\big(y(3)-y(0)\\big)=\\frac13\\left(\\frac{11^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{2^{3/2}}{3}\\right)=\\frac{11\\sqrt{11}-2\\sqrt2}{9}\\approx3.739$.",
